WEBVTT

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:25.122
Why? Somehow you seem upset
Why? Nandaka ochikonderu mitai

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:33.464
Voice, my voice. I want it to reach you
Voice, my voice. Todoketai yo kimi ni

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:41.900
Things aren't going the way you'd like
Omoi douri ni naranai koto nara

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:50.275
That might happen a lot now, but...
Ima wa takusan attarisuru kedo

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:57.282
Tomorrow, another new wind
Mata ashita wa chigau kaze

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:01.037
will blow your way
fuite kuru yo

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:05.794
Spread your arms and let your chest
Ryoute wo hirogeta mune ni

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:09.128
just feel the breeze
kanjiru mama

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:13.966
No matter what befalls us,
Nani ga osoi kakattemo

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:17.438
no matter how difficult it may be
semetatete mo

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:24.781
We'll be all right
Watashi tachi wa daijoubu

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:35.056
Very few can recognize the beginning of love.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.093
More than friends, but less than lovers...

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:43.902
Such an indefinable relationship
changes slowly over time.

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:47.706
Like the changing seasons...

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:55.906
I Want To Give You Blue Skies

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.130
Is Kenjo skipping today, too?

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:15.192
| told him to come, but...

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:19.735
Jeez... Where is he goofing off at
when he should be at practice?

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:23.274
His bad habit strikes again.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:27.437
Yes, guys who lose their
motivation as easily as him are rare.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.759
If we can win three more,
we'll make it to the Nationals.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:34.742
If he doesn't show, it will be very
detrimental to the strength of our team.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.948
Should I go look for him?

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:38.916
Yeah, sorry to make you do that.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:57.176
You're...!

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:09.722
If you're that bored, come to practice.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.633
This is such a drag.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.230
What the...

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.075
Hey! This isn't a game!

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.435
How am I supposed to practice hitting with that!?

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:35.604
Hey! Are you listening to me?

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.312
Interesting. You want to pitch for real?

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.489
Fine. I'll take you on.

00:03:55.835 --> 00:03:56.597
Got it!

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:03.767
Yes!

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.235
Horikawa!

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:13.095
Why is our manager practicing?

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.678
You didn't know, Yoshihiko?

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:18.047
She started practicing
with us a couple days ago.

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:20.117
It's news to me.

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.725
It's because you rarely come to practice.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.492
Horikawa loves baseball even more than eating.

00:04:26.933 --> 00:04:29.595
| wish someone else would be
as passionate about it as she is.

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:32.829
Well, to each his own right?

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:36.938
Horikawa's dream is to stand
on the mound at the Nationals.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:39.408
The Nationals? That's impossible!

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:42.157
Yeah. Women aren't allowed to register...

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.047
...as players in High School baseball.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.447
Does she know this?

00:04:46.586 --> 00:04:49.612
Everyone keeps saying that
someone should tell her, but...

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:53.120
...she's so determined,
no one has the heart to...

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:11.509
Horikawa, the pitcher, throws her third pitch!

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:12.709
Klank!

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:14.640
The pitcher picks up the ball!

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:17.308
Horikawa gets the ball
and throws it to first...

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.044
Ah, Kenjo!

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.610
Thank you for today.

00:05:23.523 --> 00:05:24.319
About what?

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:27.392
I'm happy you took me seriously in our match.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.262
Horikawa.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:35.532
Yes?

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.700
Want some practice?

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:40.066
Really?!

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:52.851
One more!

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:07.832
I'm not done yet!

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:13.768
Slide!

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:26.785
Thank you very much.

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:29.954
| feel like I'm one step closer to the Nationals.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:32.624
Horikawa...

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:33.551
Yes?

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:37.554
This is difficult for me to say, but...

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.626
...I need to talk with you.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.629
Talk?

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.347
| think it's better if you hear this now,

00:06:45.371 --> 00:06:47.863
rather than find out later.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:51.443
You won't be able to stand on
the mound at the Nationals.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.324
Women aren't allowed to
participate in the games...

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:57.407
...according to the regulations.

00:06:57.717 --> 00:06:59.481
B... But...

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:03.098
So, I think it might be better to
go back to being a manager or...

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:08.026
...find another club if you
like to be physically active.

00:07:08.428 --> 00:07:10.954
Baseball isn't that fun anyway, so...

00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:18.161
H-Hey! Don't cry!

00:07:21.007 --> 00:07:22.497
Oh, the poor girl.

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:26.310
Stop crying! You're making it
look like I did something!

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.804
But! But!

00:07:33.553 --> 00:07:34.543
Are you okay?

00:07:34.687 --> 00:07:35.483
Yes...

00:07:37.356 --> 00:07:39.154
You like baseball so much you'll cry?

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.090
| don't understand.

00:07:41.561 --> 00:07:43.552
Is baseball that much fun?

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.421
Baseball is every man's true love!

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:48.033
But you're a woman.

00:07:52.672 --> 00:07:55.664
Sorry! I didn't mean it like that!

00:07:56.676 --> 00:08:02.171
| really don't understand how
people can like things that much.

00:08:03.249 --> 00:08:06.184
Horikawa... why do you like baseball so much?

00:08:07.153 --> 00:08:10.487
Why? I'm not sure why.

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:12.785
| never thought about it.

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:17.124
Ever since I was little, it's been my
dream to become a baseball player.

00:08:17.497 --> 00:08:19.208
That doesn't answer my question.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:23.100
Well... There's no reason for liking something.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:26.404
You like what you like. That's all.

00:08:26.873 --> 00:08:29.501
You like what you like, eh?

00:08:29.675 --> 00:08:30.767
Kenjo?

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:34.009
| wish I had something like that.

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:39.649
| tend to be pretty good at most things,
so I don't really get excited about them.

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:41.019
Well, in that case...

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.414
...it's gotta be baseball, Kenjo!

00:08:43.923 --> 00:08:44.933
Baseball?

00:08:44.957 --> 00:08:48.552
Yes! You have such talent!

00:08:48.995 --> 00:08:52.954
If you took it seriously, getting to the
Nationals wouldn't be just a dream for you!

00:08:53.266 --> 00:08:54.859
The Nationals...

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.796
Why don't you just try it?

00:08:57.103 --> 00:09:01.199
If it doesn't feel right, you
can do something else. Plus,

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:05.354
it'd make me happy if you
were on the mound, because...

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:09.440
...you're the first batter who
opposed me seriously.

00:09:10.516 --> 00:09:14.680
| see... Baseball, eh...

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:17.453
Baseball...

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:23.996
It's a homerun!

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.728
Otowanomori Nishi High School has
done it! A last minute comeback!

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:29.866
Number four batter, Kenjo,
thrives under pressure!

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:39.309
Congratulations on advancing to the semifinals!

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.159
That's good!

00:09:44.183 --> 00:09:47.016
Tomato juice tastes great after a game!

00:09:47.253 --> 00:09:47.845
Yep!

00:09:48.387 --> 00:09:49.912
You were right.

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:53.802
Baseball is pretty fun when you get into it.

00:09:53.826 --> 00:09:57.785
Isn't it? Here, I'll give you this.

00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:02.397
A candle and a whip?

00:10:02.702 --> 00:10:03.669
That's right.

00:10:04.136 --> 00:10:06.537
You light this and swing.

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:09.151
Your batting rate will definitely go up...

00:10:09.175 --> 00:10:11.337
...if you're able to extinguish the fire!

00:10:11.477 --> 00:10:12.376
Oh...?

00:10:12.612 --> 00:10:15.190
By swinging the whip parallel to the ground...

00:10:15.214 --> 00:10:17.426
...your swing will become more consistent.

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:18.178
Really?

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:20.729
Yes. I read it in "Welcome to Baseball"...

00:10:20.753 --> 00:10:22.346
...from Minmei publishing.

00:10:22.588 --> 00:10:23.565
| see...

00:10:23.589 --> 00:10:25.387
Oh, Kenjo!

00:10:25.858 --> 00:10:27.035
Long time no see.

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:29.972
The baseball team looks
like they're pumped.

00:10:29.996 --> 00:10:31.225
AKi, Yumi.

00:10:31.731 --> 00:10:33.508
Going to the Nationals next?

00:10:33.532 --> 00:10:35.330
If we win two more.

00:10:35.434 --> 00:10:36.560
Oh...

00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:38.465
By the way, who is this?

00:10:38.671 --> 00:10:39.570
Hello!

00:10:40.239 --> 00:10:43.038
She's Horikawa... She's the team's manager.

00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:44.743
| mean, she's a player.

00:10:46.012 --> 00:10:47.036
Kenjo...

00:10:47.313 --> 00:10:49.645
| see. Nice to meet you.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:51.943
So, are you two dating?

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.481
It's not like that!

00:10:59.992 --> 00:11:02.037
Hey! He's holding a whip and a candle.

00:11:02.061 --> 00:11:03.688
Is he planning to...?

00:11:04.563 --> 00:11:05.587
Pervert!
Pervert!

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.095
What?

00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:22.439
Foul!

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.979
Only by a little bit, but it's a foul!

00:11:26.152 --> 00:11:28.052
Oto-Nishi High is leading by a single point.

00:11:28.287 --> 00:11:30.483
I'm sure they'd like another point.

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:32.920
The team's hopes are on Kenjo's swing.

00:11:46.405 --> 00:11:51.070
This sucks... Of course this happens
when baseball was getting fun...

00:11:51.577 --> 00:11:53.909
They won the match after you were injured.

00:11:54.346 --> 00:11:57.043
It doesn't matter! Look at my arm!

00:11:57.349 --> 00:11:59.477
They told me I shouldn't move it for a while!

00:11:59.852 --> 00:12:02.082
They told me I won't heal in
time for the final game.

00:12:02.354 --> 00:12:04.186
You'll be able to be in the match!

00:12:05.558 --> 00:12:07.151
As a base coach.

00:12:07.359 --> 00:12:09.293
That doesn't mean anything.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.347
If I knew this was going to happen,

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:21.635
| wouldn't have gotten so into it.

00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:24.509
If I knew I was going to regret it this much...

00:12:24.944 --> 00:12:26.021
Kenjo.

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:28.480
| quit! I'm quitting baseball.

00:12:30.049 --> 00:12:31.380
You idiot!

00:12:32.785 --> 00:12:36.278
Stop acting so pathetic over getting hit by a ball!

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:39.182
You should be thankful you're
able to be on the field!

00:12:39.492 --> 00:12:45.693
I... was terrible at baseball, but I never quit.

00:12:45.865 --> 00:12:48.994
But you... But you...

00:12:53.572 --> 00:12:54.334
I'm sorry.

00:12:55.674 --> 00:12:57.642
| apologize.

00:12:58.744 --> 00:13:01.372
I'll be a base coach for the final match.

00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:07.279
Victory!

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:28.766
Safe!

00:13:32.611 --> 00:13:33.476
Out!

00:13:35.147 --> 00:13:36.376
Game set!

00:14:23.028 --> 00:14:24.894
Ah, Kenjo!

00:14:29.935 --> 00:14:34.600
What's wrong, Kenjo? You seem down.

00:14:35.507 --> 00:14:39.375
I've been spacing out since the Nationals.

00:14:39.745 --> 00:14:41.008
| wonder why?

00:14:41.247 --> 00:14:44.376
Maybe it's because you were so into it?

00:14:44.483 --> 00:14:45.450
Maybe...

00:14:45.784 --> 00:14:48.776
Is there anything else you can get into?

00:14:48.988 --> 00:14:51.013
| can't switch gears that easily...

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:54.357
It's not like I have any hobbies either...

00:14:56.896 --> 00:14:57.806
I got it!

00:14:57.830 --> 00:15:00.299
Kenjo, is your arm okay now?

00:15:00.666 --> 00:15:02.430
Yeah, I'm fully recovered.

00:15:02.835 --> 00:15:06.032
Then let's go to the pool together tomorrow!

00:15:07.506 --> 00:15:09.317
The games are over,

00:15:09.341 --> 00:15:12.003
but you're going get out
of shape if you're slacking.

00:15:12.244 --> 00:15:15.991
It'll be good to go swim and
work your entire body...

00:15:16.015 --> 00:15:17.983
...from a sports medicine point of view.

00:15:18.751 --> 00:15:19.775
The pool...

00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:20.886
Yes, the pool!

00:15:22.187 --> 00:15:23.086
Let's go then!

00:15:23.188 --> 00:15:23.780
Yes!

00:15:33.332 --> 00:15:34.197
Ready!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:36.263
What is that?

00:15:39.471 --> 00:15:42.202
It's because I can't swim.

00:15:53.085 --> 00:15:54.143
That's cold!

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.227
Hey, Horikawa. I was wondering...

00:16:02.328 --> 00:16:02.920
Yes?

00:16:03.162 --> 00:16:05.640
This place may have a pool,

00:16:05.664 --> 00:16:09.794
but it doesn't seem like where you'd
go for sports medicine and a workout.

00:16:11.036 --> 00:16:12.731
I-It's okay!

00:16:13.005 --> 00:16:17.719
Plus, even pro-athletes need
to relax at places like this!

00:16:17.743 --> 00:16:18.853
| see...

00:16:18.877 --> 00:16:22.336
Well, if you put it that way, this is fun too, so...

00:16:22.414 --> 00:16:23.848
Isn't it? Isn't it?

00:16:26.418 --> 00:16:27.647
What's wrong?

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:29.287
I'm going to go swim!

00:16:39.531 --> 00:16:41.276
I'm tired...

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:44.201
Swimming five thousand meters
all at once will do that.

00:16:44.737 --> 00:16:47.638
The station isn't too far. You can do it.

00:16:48.140 --> 00:16:48.868
Okay...

00:16:59.852 --> 00:17:00.648
Yank!

00:17:03.122 --> 00:17:04.749
| had a lot of fun today.

00:17:04.857 --> 00:17:09.021
I'm glad! It makes me happy
when I see you smile!

00:17:09.228 --> 00:17:11.424
How about going to the
amusement park next time?

00:17:12.698 --> 00:17:16.430
How about going to Jyunna Morio's
concert? Do you know Mori-Jyun?

00:17:16.535 --> 00:17:20.415
H-Hey, amusement parks and concerts
have nothing to do with baseball.

00:17:20.439 --> 00:17:24.876
Yeah, but the pool didn't have
anything to do with it either.

00:17:28.447 --> 00:17:29.039
See you!

00:17:30.416 --> 00:17:32.407
Hey wait, Horikawa!

00:17:41.026 --> 00:17:41.857
Hello?

00:17:42.428 --> 00:17:43.589
It's me, Kenjo.

00:17:44.063 --> 00:17:46.395
Kenjo! What's wrong?

00:17:46.732 --> 00:17:48.598
Can you talk?

00:17:49.034 --> 00:17:50.832
Yes. What is it?

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.502
Thanks for today.

00:17:54.406 --> 00:17:55.840
For taking me out today...

00:17:56.308 --> 00:17:58.953
You did it to cheer me up, right?

00:17:58.977 --> 00:17:59.876
Oh... Yes...

00:18:00.612 --> 00:18:02.490
Thanks to you, I'm feeling much better.

00:18:02.514 --> 00:18:03.606
I'm glad.

00:18:03.982 --> 00:18:07.316
It seems like you're always helping me out.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:09.647
Baseball was fun...

00:18:10.155 --> 00:18:12.681
You showed me how fun it can be
to be passionate about something.

00:18:12.925 --> 00:18:14.256
I really appreciate it.

00:18:14.993 --> 00:18:16.304
You don't need to...

00:18:16.328 --> 00:18:17.261
So...

00:18:17.996 --> 00:18:18.554
Yes?

00:18:18.931 --> 00:18:23.869
| want to give something back, but
| have no idea what I can do for you.

00:18:24.236 --> 00:18:25.829
Do you have any requests?

00:18:26.405 --> 00:18:28.999
| can't think of anything... It's so sudden...

00:18:30.109 --> 00:18:32.305
Actually, I do have a request!

00:18:42.921 --> 00:18:45.481
Are you sure this will do?

00:18:45.624 --> 00:18:46.250
Yes!

00:18:46.525 --> 00:18:50.359
| wasn't fully satisfied with our
last match, so I'd like a do over!

00:18:50.529 --> 00:18:51.758
Thank you!

00:18:52.264 --> 00:18:55.097
All right! I'm going to give it all I've got!

00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:56.123
Yes!

00:19:10.482 --> 00:19:12.450
In and low. Strike.

00:19:19.291 --> 00:19:20.656
Bring it on!

00:19:30.035 --> 00:19:32.265
Center! Strike two!

00:19:35.274 --> 00:19:35.934
Time out!

00:19:47.553 --> 00:19:51.581
What's wrong? Both pitches were easy hits...

00:19:55.327 --> 00:19:57.557
Is it because it's her?

00:20:04.903 --> 00:20:05.631
This is the last!

00:20:46.111 --> 00:20:49.137
Fgetit. [like her...

00:20:50.749 --> 00:20:52.945
Very few can recognize the beginning of love.

00:20:53.719 --> 00:20:56.051
More than friends, but less than lovers...

00:20:56.755 --> 00:21:01.716
Such an indefinable relationship
changes slowly over time.

00:21:04.896 --> 00:21:06.591
Got it!

00:21:09.234 --> 00:21:12.397
Like the changing seasons...

00:21:14.373 --> 00:21:15.340
You're out!

00:21:17.976 --> 00:21:19.137
Nice catch.

00:21:31.823 --> 00:21:34.702
There's no reason,
Riyuu nanka nakute

00:21:34.726 --> 00:21:40.495
we're just happy when we're together
issho nara ureshiku nattari

00:21:41.066 --> 00:21:49.066
Somehow we connect, everyone together
Nanto naku tsuuji au minna ga ii ne

00:21:57.416 --> 00:22:02.664
We lay down on the riverbed
Kawara no shamen nekoron da

00:22:02.688 --> 00:22:05.623
stretching our arms and legs
teashi wo nobashite

00:22:06.725 --> 00:22:14.598
Birds flew above our heads
Atama no ue wo tori tachi ga tobitatta

00:22:16.034 --> 00:22:20.682
I just look up at the sky
Futo miageta kyou no sora

00:22:20.706 --> 00:22:23.732
it seems to spread forever
doko mademo hirogaru

00:22:24.209 --> 00:22:29.390
All the things bothering me
